WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.922 --> 00:00:01.989
CNN primetime.

00:00:02.123 --> 00:00:03.891
Joe Biden abroad.

00:00:03.891 --> 00:00:05.293
That areas tomorrow at 9:00 P.M.

00:00:05.426 --> 00:00:06.394
Eastern right here on CNN.

00:00:06.527 --> 00:00:07.094
Don't miss it.

00:00:07.228 --> 00:00:08.896
&gt;&gt;&gt; One day before president

00:00:09.030 --> 00:00:10.398
Biden's visit to Selma, Alabama,

00:00:10.531 --> 00:00:13.434
his predecessor headlined the

00:00:13.567 --> 00:00:14.135
conservative political action

00:00:14.268 --> 00:00:15.269
conference in Maryland just

00:00:15.403 --> 00:00:15.903
outside of Washington.

00:00:16.037 --> 00:00:17.338
Over the course of nearly two

00:00:17.471 --> 00:00:18.272
hours, former president Donald

00:00:18.406 --> 00:00:20.975
Trump lashed out at Biden and

00:00:21.108 --> 00:00:23.911
many Republicans, bemoaned

00:00:23.911 --> 00:00:25.947
ongoing investigations into

00:00:26.080 --> 00:00:26.681
himself, vowed he won't drop out

00:00:26.814 --> 00:00:27.348
of the race even if he's

00:00:27.481 --> 00:00:30.451
indicted, and signaled how he

00:00:30.584 --> 00:00:31.218
might campaign in the coming

00:00:31.352 --> 00:00:32.253
months to be elected again.

00:00:32.386 --> 00:00:34.522
Here's what he said.

00:00:34.655 --> 00:00:39.927
&gt;&gt; In 2016, I declared I am your

00:00:40.027 --> 00:00:40.194
voice.

00:00:40.328 --> 00:00:44.398
Today I add, I am your warrior.

00:00:44.532 --> 00:00:45.199
I am your justice.

00:00:45.333 --> 00:00:46.534
And for those who have been

00:00:46.667 --> 00:00:49.270
wronged and betrayed, I am your

00:00:49.403 --> 00:00:49.937
retribution.

00:00:49.937 --> 00:00:51.939
I am your retribution.

00:00:51.939 --> 00:00:53.574
&gt;&gt; Joining me now, former trump

00:00:53.941 --> 00:00:54.742
white house press secretary

00:00:54.875 --> 00:00:56.344
Stephanie Grisham and Olivia

00:00:56.477 --> 00:00:58.312
troye, a former adviser to vice

00:00:58.446 --> 00:00:59.947
president Mike pence.

00:00:59.981 --> 00:01:01.515
Stephanie, let me start with

00:01:01.949 --> 00:01:02.949
you.

00:01:01.949 --> 00:01:03.951
You know, it's so easy to blow

00:01:04.018 --> 00:01:06.153
off trump's bluster and some of

00:01:06.287 --> 00:01:07.121
the things that he says.

00:01:07.254 --> 00:01:10.691
But when he talks about

00:01:10.825 --> 00:01:13.961
retribution and talking about

00:01:13.961 --> 00:01:16.397
revenge, what did you make of

00:01:16.530 --> 00:01:16.697
that?

00:01:16.831 --> 00:01:17.965
&gt;&gt; Well, you know, it's

00:01:17.965 --> 00:01:19.033
something I've been saying for

00:01:19.166 --> 00:01:20.201
quite a while, that this is

00:01:20.334 --> 00:01:22.770
going to be a revenge tour for

00:01:22.903 --> 00:01:23.971
the former president.

00:01:23.971 --> 00:01:25.406
But, you know, I wondered

00:01:25.539 --> 00:01:26.607
specifically with regard to what

00:01:26.741 --> 00:01:29.377
he said, who decides who needs

00:01:29.510 --> 00:01:29.977
the retribution?

00:01:29.977 --> 00:01:31.579
Who's going to decide who's been

00:01:31.979 --> 00:01:32.113
mistreated?

00:01:32.113 --> 00:01:33.547
I mean what about all the people

00:01:33.981 --> 00:01:35.016
who suffered or had family

00:01:35.149 --> 00:01:36.317
members pass away from covid?

00:01:36.450 --> 00:01:38.119
Are you going to be retribution

00:01:38.252 --> 00:01:39.120
for that?

00:01:39.253 --> 00:01:40.488
You had a hand in that.

00:01:40.621 --> 00:01:42.123
So I think it was, as you just

00:01:42.256 --> 00:01:43.657
said, a lot of bluster for him.

00:01:43.991 --> 00:01:45.626
But it's what his base wants to

00:01:45.993 --> 00:01:46.794
hear, and I think it's something

00:01:46.927 --> 00:01:49.096
that should be taken seriously.

00:01:49.230 --> 00:01:50.865
A lot of people right now, I

00:01:50.998 --> 00:01:52.166
think, are rolling their eyes

00:01:52.299 --> 00:01:53.167
and saying that's just trump

00:01:53.300 --> 00:01:54.001
being trump.

00:01:54.001 --> 00:01:55.002
But this is important.

00:01:55.136 --> 00:01:56.303
We need to really pay attention

00:01:56.437 --> 00:01:58.005
to what he's saying and realize

00:01:58.005 --> 00:01:59.173
we're not going to get the same

00:01:59.306 --> 00:01:59.607
Donald Trump.

00:02:00.007 --> 00:02:01.275
We're going to get a more angry

00:02:01.409 --> 00:02:02.410
and vengeful Donald Trump if he

00:02:02.543 --> 00:02:04.011
should take office.

00:02:04.145 --> 00:02:06.147
&gt;&gt; Right, if that's even

00:02:06.280 --> 00:02:06.514
possible.

00:02:06.647 --> 00:02:09.016
And Olivia, speaking earlier

00:02:09.150 --> 00:02:10.684
this past week with CBS news,

00:02:10.818 --> 00:02:12.253
your former boss, Mike pence,

00:02:12.386 --> 00:02:14.655
twice declined to commit to

00:02:14.789 --> 00:02:15.589
supporting Donald Trump.

00:02:16.023 --> 00:02:19.060
That was notable, if he's the

00:02:19.193 --> 00:02:20.027
GOP nominee.

00:02:20.027 --> 00:02:21.128
Listen to what he had to say.

00:02:21.262 --> 00:02:22.630
&gt;&gt; Well, I think we'll have

00:02:22.763 --> 00:02:26.367
better choices, and I really

00:02:26.500 --> 00:02:30.037
trust Republican voters to sort

00:02:30.071 --> 00:02:30.538
it out.

00:02:30.671 --> 00:02:32.039
&gt;&gt; Yeah, that's not really

00:02:32.173 --> 00:02:33.140
committing to supporting trump.

00:02:33.274 --> 00:02:36.043
What did you think of that,

00:02:36.110 --> 00:02:36.310
Olivia?

00:02:36.444 --> 00:02:42.716
&gt;&gt; Well, I think -- you know,

00:02:42.850 --> 00:02:44.051
the reality is that is where the

00:02:44.051 --> 00:02:45.086
Republican party is.

00:02:45.219 --> 00:02:47.221
Like Stephanie said, I don't

00:02:47.354 --> 00:02:47.688
discount trump.

00:02:48.055 --> 00:02:48.622
He is the front-runner.

00:02:48.756 --> 00:02:50.825
I think pence is hoping, hey,

00:02:50.958 --> 00:02:51.425
I'm a better choice.

00:02:51.559 --> 00:02:54.061
The choice is me.

00:02:54.195 --> 00:02:56.130
And I strongly believe that he

00:02:56.263 --> 00:02:56.664
will run.

00:02:56.797 --> 00:02:59.600
But I think the reality is that

00:02:59.733 --> 00:03:02.069
the past victory there in the

00:03:02.136 --> 00:03:03.604
Republican lane is very narrow

00:03:03.737 --> 00:03:04.638
for these other candidates

00:03:04.772 --> 00:03:05.272
outside of trump.

00:03:05.406 --> 00:03:06.674
And I think the Republican party

00:03:06.807 --> 00:03:08.742
needs to decide whether they're

00:03:08.876 --> 00:03:10.077
willing to support someone else

00:03:10.077 --> 00:03:12.413
and really back that candidate.

00:03:12.546 --> 00:03:14.348
&gt;&gt; And I guess I want to ask you

00:03:14.482 --> 00:03:16.784
both just as a follow-up to

00:03:16.917 --> 00:03:18.085
that, I mean can you believe

00:03:18.085 --> 00:03:19.520
where we are right now, coming

00:03:19.653 --> 00:03:21.755
out of CPAC, where Donald

00:03:22.089 --> 00:03:25.459
Trump -- obviously he won the

00:03:25.593 --> 00:03:26.894
unscientific straw poll at CPAC,

00:03:27.027 --> 00:03:28.329
but he's leading in all of the

00:03:28.462 --> 00:03:28.729
polls.

00:03:28.863 --> 00:03:30.097
Stephanie, as his former white

00:03:30.097 --> 00:03:30.931
house secretary, and I know you

00:03:31.065 --> 00:03:32.533
don't want to see him back in

00:03:32.666 --> 00:03:34.301
the oval office ever again, are

00:03:34.435 --> 00:03:36.103
you at all surprised that trump

00:03:36.137 --> 00:03:38.139
is in this position where he --

00:03:38.272 --> 00:03:40.107
I mean Larry hogan decided today

00:03:40.174 --> 00:03:42.209
he's not going to run.

00:03:42.343 --> 00:03:43.677
There aren't a lot of takers in

00:03:44.111 --> 00:03:45.779
terms of wanting to take on

00:03:46.113 --> 00:03:46.213
Donald Trump.

00:03:46.347 --> 00:03:48.115
He may get this nomination

00:03:48.115 --> 00:03:48.182
again.

00:03:48.315 --> 00:03:50.518
What do you think about that?

00:03:50.651 --> 00:03:51.785
&gt;&gt; Well, I'm obviously not

00:03:52.119 --> 00:03:53.487
happy, and I have committed to

00:03:53.621 --> 00:03:55.222
doing all I can to try and

00:03:55.356 --> 00:03:56.490
ensure that that doesn't happen

00:03:56.624 --> 00:03:58.359
by just talking to people and

00:03:58.492 --> 00:03:59.793
educating people on who he

00:04:00.127 --> 00:04:00.528
really is.

00:04:00.661 --> 00:04:02.830
But, you know, I think that what

00:04:02.963 --> 00:04:04.899
Asa Hutchinson did was smart.

00:04:05.032 --> 00:04:06.634
I think he really saw that he

00:04:06.767 --> 00:04:08.135
had no path to victory, and I

00:04:08.135 --> 00:04:09.470
think -- well, I hope --

00:04:09.603 --> 00:04:10.337
&gt;&gt; Larry hogan.

00:04:10.471 --> 00:04:11.539
&gt;&gt; I'm sorry, yes.

00:04:11.672 --> 00:04:14.842
I think other people who are

00:04:14.975 --> 00:04:16.610
wanting to maybe jump into the

00:04:16.744 --> 00:04:18.145
race, I hope they have that kind

00:04:18.145 --> 00:04:19.747
of look-within moment because,

00:04:20.147 --> 00:04:21.148
again, as we've all talked about

00:04:21.282 --> 00:04:22.950
many times, back in 2016, the

00:04:23.083 --> 00:04:24.718
reason trump won the primary was

00:04:24.852 --> 00:04:26.353
because the field was so big.

00:04:26.487 --> 00:04:27.521
I do believe if somebody like

00:04:27.655 --> 00:04:30.457
Ron Desantis gets in, it's early

00:04:30.591 --> 00:04:31.792
yet, so these polls -- I know

00:04:32.159 --> 00:04:33.427
they do have trump ahead, but I

00:04:33.561 --> 00:04:34.528
do believe if somebody really

00:04:34.662 --> 00:04:36.163
gets in and is willing to take

00:04:36.163 --> 00:04:38.165
him on, I think there's a

00:04:38.165 --> 00:04:38.832
fighting chance there.

00:04:38.966 --> 00:04:40.601
But I'm definitely worried.

00:04:40.734 --> 00:04:42.169
I'm definitely concerned about,

00:04:42.169 --> 00:04:46.373
you know, how strong he is still

00:04:46.507 --> 00:04:47.074
after everything that people

00:04:47.208 --> 00:04:50.177
have seen over and over.

00:04:50.177 --> 00:04:51.145
&gt;&gt; Olivia, Stephanie mentioned

00:04:51.278 --> 00:04:52.546
Ron Desantis.

00:04:52.680 --> 00:04:53.781
What do you think?

00:04:53.914 --> 00:04:55.015
Do you think he could

00:04:55.149 --> 00:04:55.783
potentially knock trump out of

00:04:56.183 --> 00:04:57.184
this spot that he's in right

00:04:57.318 --> 00:04:58.385
now, which really he's the

00:04:58.519 --> 00:04:59.119
front-runner right now.

00:04:59.253 --> 00:05:00.654
He's the man to beat.

00:05:00.788 --> 00:05:02.823
I know there's a long way to go,

00:05:02.957 --> 00:05:04.225
but I mean many people consider

00:05:04.358 --> 00:05:06.193
the Florida governor the

00:05:06.193 --> 00:05:07.795
strongest opponent trump could

00:05:08.195 --> 00:05:08.829
face for the nomination.

00:05:08.963 --> 00:05:10.197
But do you think he could knock

00:05:10.264 --> 00:05:12.933
him out of that spot?

00:05:13.067 --> 00:05:14.868
&gt;&gt; I think it will be very hard.

00:05:15.002 --> 00:05:16.971
I think once Desantis gets

00:05:17.104 --> 00:05:19.139
going, I don't think he's as

00:05:19.273 --> 00:05:19.506
appealing.

00:05:19.640 --> 00:05:22.209
He doesn't have the charisma, so

00:05:22.343 --> 00:05:24.211
to speak, that trump has, that

00:05:24.211 --> 00:05:25.446
kind of draw, that fiery brand,

00:05:25.579 --> 00:05:26.213
I would say.

00:05:26.447 --> 00:05:27.681
I actually don't see the two of

00:05:27.815 --> 00:05:28.882
them as being different people.

00:05:30.251 --> 00:05:32.219
I know that many of my

00:05:32.319 --> 00:05:33.120
Republican colleagues will say,

00:05:33.254 --> 00:05:34.888
oh, Desantis is so much better.

00:05:35.022 --> 00:05:36.223
I don't see his politics as very

00:05:36.323 --> 00:05:37.191
different than trumpism.

00:05:37.324 --> 00:05:38.225
He is trumpism.

00:05:38.225 --> 00:05:39.793
He's just, you know, got a

00:05:40.227 --> 00:05:42.229
different cloak wrapped around

00:05:42.229 --> 00:05:42.296
him.

00:05:42.429 --> 00:05:44.365
But I think it's a possibility.

00:05:44.498 --> 00:05:45.799
Do I see it?

00:05:46.233 --> 00:05:48.302
Not right now.

00:05:48.435 --> 00:05:50.237
&gt;&gt; And, Stephanie, trump said

00:05:50.237 --> 00:05:51.538
yesterday to reporters that he's

00:05:51.672 --> 00:05:53.107
going to run again no matter

00:05:53.240 --> 00:05:55.776
what, even if he's indicted.

00:05:55.909 --> 00:05:56.810
What are your thoughts?

00:05:56.944 --> 00:05:58.279
Do you think that there's a

00:05:58.412 --> 00:06:00.247
chance that we will see an

00:06:00.247 --> 00:06:02.249
indictment of Donald Trump, or

00:06:02.249 --> 00:06:03.751
did the justice department,

00:06:03.884 --> 00:06:05.819
various authorities just kind of

00:06:06.253 --> 00:06:07.288
miss their chance to do that, to

00:06:07.421 --> 00:06:08.422
bring an indictment?

00:06:08.555 --> 00:06:10.257
&gt;&gt; Well, I don't want to say

00:06:10.257 --> 00:06:11.125
that they missed their chance.

00:06:11.258 --> 00:06:12.793
As we all know, the wheels of

00:06:12.926 --> 00:06:14.261
justice move very, very slow.

00:06:14.261 --> 00:06:16.630
And I do believe truly that the

00:06:16.764 --> 00:06:17.364
justice department wants to do

00:06:17.498 --> 00:06:18.666
this the right way.

00:06:18.799 --> 00:06:20.267
I don't believe we're going to

00:06:20.267 --> 00:06:21.568
see him get indicted.

00:06:21.702 --> 00:06:22.569
I really don't.

00:06:22.703 --> 00:06:24.271
I think that at this point, it

00:06:24.305 --> 00:06:26.273
will all just be political,

00:06:26.340 --> 00:06:27.374
political, political according

00:06:27.508 --> 00:06:29.443
to, you know, the Republican

00:06:29.576 --> 00:06:29.743
party.

00:06:29.877 --> 00:06:31.011
But to answer your question, the

00:06:31.145 --> 00:06:32.279
fact that he said that, you

00:06:32.313 --> 00:06:33.480
know, he would continue to run

00:06:33.614 --> 00:06:35.149
even if indicted, that did not

00:06:35.282 --> 00:06:36.817
surprise me at all.

00:06:36.950 --> 00:06:37.618
That was prime trump.

00:06:37.751 --> 00:06:38.819
He's doubling down.

00:06:38.952 --> 00:06:40.554
This is how he says he's

00:06:40.688 --> 00:06:41.455
completely innocent.

00:06:41.588 --> 00:06:42.923
And he just, you know -- he

00:06:43.057 --> 00:06:46.293
doesn't care about the justice

00:06:46.293 --> 00:06:46.427
system.

00:06:46.560 --> 00:06:46.894
He doesn't care.

00:06:47.027 --> 00:06:48.295
He gets away with everything, so

00:06:48.362 --> 00:06:50.297
why would he be suddenly like,

00:06:50.364 --> 00:06:53.200
I'm going to drop out?

00:06:53.334 --> 00:06:55.469
&gt;&gt; Olivia, final thought to you.

00:06:55.602 --> 00:06:58.472
&gt;&gt; Yeah, what are we going to

00:06:58.605 --> 00:06:58.772
have?

00:06:58.906 --> 00:07:00.374
We're going to have Donald

00:07:00.507 --> 00:07:03.210
corleone running for the

00:07:03.344 --> 00:07:04.611
president of the United States?

00:07:04.745 --> 00:07:06.313
This is embarrassing if he does

00:07:06.313 --> 00:07:07.247
get indicted, and that would be

00:07:07.381 --> 00:07:08.315
the case.

00:07:08.382 --> 00:07:09.516
I agree with Stephanie.

00:07:09.650 --> 00:07:10.884
I see him doubling down.

00:07:11.018 --> 00:07:12.319
Look, there's a reason that Jim

00:07:12.319 --> 00:07:13.020
Jordan and all these Republicans

00:07:13.153 --> 00:07:16.323
on the hill have this

00:07:16.323 --> 00:07:17.858
weaponization of the U.S.

00:07:17.991 --> 00:07:18.325
Government.

00:07:18.392 --> 00:07:19.893
That is all in my opinion part

00:07:20.327 --> 00:07:20.994
of the strategic plan of how

00:07:21.128 --> 00:07:22.596
they will spin this.

